# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
autotaggerr

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# config directory
/config

# web UI dependencies (installed via `npm ci` in webui/)
/webui/node_modules
# NOTE: web/dist (the built SPA) is intentionally NOT ignored — the Go binary
# embeds it via go:embed, so committing it keeps `go build ./...` working without
# a Node toolchain. CI rebuilds it from webui/ before every Go step.
